            <ArticleTitle>Laryngeal candidiasis: our experience from sixty biopsy specimens.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/coa.13034</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Persistent throat symptoms, such as dysphonia, globus and throat pain, are highly prevalent and are a significant cause of morbidity(1) . In a number of cases a clear cause of these symptoms is not identified and many patients are treated empirically with lifestyle advice and/or anti-reflux medication(2) . This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
